\f0\fs24 \cf2 The four doors opening onto the grand salon are an architectural marvel, framed by two majestic stucco pilasters designed to mimic the stone of the monumental fireplace and ensure perfect visual continuity. The sculptural decoration of the pilasters was conceived by Giuseppe himself, who left his signature on one of them: 
\f1\i "Jo de Bagatis Formis."
\f0\i0  The museum\'92s archive preserves the preparatory drawings, executed with meticulous compositional care. These studies, made with ink and black pencil, reveal the thoughtful planning behind these elements, inspired by historical sources documented in photographs also held in the archive.}